{"term":"postulate","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:82c08a0fec50ffb242","definition":"Something assumed without proof as being self-evident or generally accepted, especially when used as a basis for an argument. Sometimes distinguished from axioms as being relevant to a particular science or context, rather than universally true, and following from other axioms rather than being an absolute assumption.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Bertrand's postulate","Hebb's postulate","Koch's postulate","parallel postulate","triangle postulate","universal postulate","postulatory"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/postulate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c9439c935efe63b9be","definition":"A fundamental element; a basic principle.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Bertrand's postulate","Hebb's postulate","Koch's postulate","parallel postulate","triangle postulate","universal postulate","postulatory"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/postulate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d1486b20e43d3cf0be","definition":"An axiom.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Bertrand's postulate","Hebb's postulate","Koch's postulate","parallel postulate","triangle postulate","universal postulate","postulatory"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/postulate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f952c403985e1172f7","definition":"A requirement; a prerequisite.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Bertrand's postulate","Hebb's postulate","Koch's postulate","parallel postulate","triangle postulate","universal postulate","postulatory"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/postulate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ae89a5507c20c680d5","definition":"To assume as a truthful or accurate premise or axiom, especially as a basis of an argument.","example":"1883, Benedictus de Spinoza, translated by R. H. M. Elwes, Ethics, Part 3, Prop. XXII,\nBut this pleasure or pain is postulated to come to us accompanied by the idea of an external cause; […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Bertrand's postulate","Hebb's postulate","Koch's postulate","parallel postulate","triangle postulate","universal postulate","postulatory","postulation","postulational","repostulate","unpostulated"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/postulate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5c1d605f3193ec8bd9","definition":"To appoint or request one's appointment to an ecclesiastical office.","example":"[A]lthough Douglas was postulated to it [the Abbacy of Arbroath], and signed letters and papers under this designation his nomination […] was never completed.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive, historical","register":"ambitransitive, historical","wordFamily":["Bertrand's postulate","Hebb's postulate","Koch's postulate","parallel postulate","triangle postulate","universal postulate","postulatory","postulation","postulational","repostulate","unpostulated"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/postulate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9de56a64fcedbc05a5","definition":"To request, demand or claim for oneself.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive, obsolete","register":"ambitransitive, obsolete","wordFamily":["Bertrand's postulate","Hebb's postulate","Koch's postulate","parallel postulate","triangle postulate","universal postulate","postulatory","postulation","postulational","repostulate","unpostulated"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/postulate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1a9cfa30d1af4382ac","definition":"Alternative form of postulated, past participle of postulate.","example":"Quoth he, What Nature can afford,\nI shall produce upon my word ;\nAnd if she ever gave that boon\nTo man, I'll prove that I have one ;\nI mean, by postulate Illation,\nWhen you shall offer just occasion ;[…]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"alt-of, alternative, obsolete","register":"alt-of, alternative, obsolete","wordFamily":["Bertrand's postulate","Hebb's postulate","Koch's postulate","parallel postulate","triangle postulate","universal postulate","postulatory","postulation","postulational","repostulate","unpostulated"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/postulate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈpɒstjʊlət/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/fb/En-us-postulate-verb.ogg/En-us-postulate-verb.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["Bertrand's postulate","Hebb's postulate","Koch's postulate","parallel postulate","triangle postulate","universal postulate","postulatory","postulation","postulational","repostulate","unpostulated"]}